{"description":"Add the one-shot `eka migrate v2`: scan the live store, unlink every `assigned-to` edge and retire every `mbr` line, forward-only (append-only, no hard delete), idempotent (a re-run is a no-op), with a dry-run and a deterministic report of what changed. Take a pre-migration snapshot/backup; state that forward-only is a deliberate design choice (no automatic rollback). Handle mixed-version clients that may re-write edges after a migration, and cover `shr` sharing objects held in other stores.","acceptanceCriteria":"`eka migrate v2 --dry-run` reports the `assigned-to` edges and `mbr` lines that would change, writing nothing; a pre-migration backup/snapshot is produced.\nA real run retires `mbr` lines and removes `assigned-to` edges forward-only.\nRe-running is a no-op; reading pre-migration snapshots still works.\nMixed-version-client behaviour is documented and tested (a re-written edge after migration is detected).\nPer-store scope is documented; `shr` sharing-object impact is covered.\nStore integrity report is clean after migration."}